# PHP 7.3 Compatible Syntax

The backend runs on Cafe24's **PHP 7.3**. Do not use syntax exclusive to 7.4+ / 8.x.

## Forbidden Syntax

| Feature                   | Minimum Version | Alternative                  |
| ------------------------- | --------------- | ---------------------------- |
| Arrow functions `fn()`    | 7.4             | `function () { ... }`        |
| `??=`                     | 7.4             | `$x = $x ?? $default`        |
| Array spread `[...$arr]`  | 7.4             | `array_merge()`              |
| Typed properties          | 7.4             | Regular properties + PHPDoc  |
| `match`                   | 8.0             | `switch`                     |
| Nullsafe `?->`            | 8.0             | Null check before access     |
| Named arguments           | 8.0             | Positional arguments         |
| Union types `string\|int` | 8.0             | PHPDoc `@param`              |
| Constructor promotion     | 8.0             | Explicit property assignment |
| Attributes `#[...]`       | 8.0             | Prohibited                   |

## Example

```php
// ❌ BAD — PHP 7.4+ (fatal error at parse stage → API 500)
$files = array_map(
    static fn (array $file): array => board_format_attachment_meta($file, $bo_table),
    $file_rows
);

// ✅ GOOD — PHP 7.3 compatible
$files = array_map(function (array $file) use ($bo_table): array {
    return board_format_attachment_meta($file, $bo_table);
}, $file_rows);
```

## Checks During Writing / Review

- After modifying `backend/**/*.php`, search for `static fn`, `fn(`, `match(`, `??=`, `?->`.
- Write against the **7.3 baseline** even if the local PHP version is 8.x.
- Run `php -l filename.php` for syntax checking before deployment.
